Description: Hand a 3D video's views to the compositor at their own resolution
 .
 The video layer of a 3D video was twice the item's width in pixels, so
 mpv scaled both views into the window and the compositor got views the
 program had already resized: a half top-and-bottom 1920x1080 video went
 as two 1280x720 views in a 1280x720 item.
 .
 The layer's buffer is now the frame mpv outputs, both views at the
 resolution they have (that video as one 3840x540 buffer), and the
 viewport, which has the size of one view in the item, gives the
 compositor the one resize. mpv keeps no aspect of its own while the
 layer holds a 3D video, so it draws the frame onto the whole buffer
 sample for sample; the layer's rectangle has the video's shape, and
 mpv's own keepaspect comes back with the next 2D video.
